mfd: retu: Tahvo charger off; all IRQs; ADC; /dev/retu and /dev/tahvo

- Tahvo: charge PWM (CHGCURR) to 0 at probe (logging CHGCURR/CHGCTL as
  found), on shutdown/reboot/kexec and on panic. Nothing in the kernel
  manages charging; Maemo's BME does it from userspace.
- All 16 Retu and 8 Tahvo interrupt sources in the regmap-irq chips.
- retu_read_adc() (with the Vilma battery voltage quirk),
  retu_update_bits(), retu_irq_virq().
- CONFIG_MFD_RETU_USER: Nokia's retu-user/tahvo-user ioctl ABI, which
  Maemo's BME uses, on top of retu-mfd, as misc minors 62 and 63
  (linuxrc parses /proc/misc in a way that needs minors below 100).
